cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "Symmetry Entropy: orbit entropy, projection entropy, and asymmetry cost (SYNTHETIC classical emulation)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Brisson"
    given-names: "Jean-François"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374"
    affiliation: "Spark AI NLP, Fredericton, New Brunswick, Canada"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-15"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/symmetry-entropy"
abstract: >-
  SYNTHETIC. Standard-library Python plus NumPy: symmetry entropy
  measures what a projection can resolve, what it must store, and what
  it is blind to. Orbit entropy log2(|orbit|) under D4 on 4x4 patterns
  (asymmetric 3 bits, blocks 1 bit, ring and cross 0 bits); projection
  entropy, the Shannon entropy of the Born weights after projecting onto
  a stored subspace (0 bits clean, 0.618 bits at sigma 0.25, 1.270 bits
  at sigma 0.75, 1.581 bits Haar-random); asymmetry cost S(twirl) - S(rho)
  under Pauli {I, X} (|0> 1 bit, |+> 0 bits); self-determinism factor
  D = <psi|P|psi> (1 for a clean stored probe, 0 for a kernel probe,
  strictly between for noisy and random probes); honeycomb / bee-hexagon
  extension (D6 orbit entropy: asymmetric hexagonal pattern 3.585 bits,
  honeycomb cell 0 bits; honeycomb patch bipartite, 24 vertices, 30 edges;
  Hales: hexagon perimeter 3.7224 < square 4.0000 < triangle 4.5590;
  Shipman alpha transition at 1/sqrt(3) = 0.5774; radical-pair compass
  toy: 0.3763 along z vs 0.2524 along x at 50 uT). Eight falsifiable
  claims, all measured. No headline claim is emitted. No speedup, no Bell
  violation, no hardware data, no claim about physical reality. Shipman
  is a documented correlation with an unproven mechanism; the radical-pair
  model is a one-nucleus toy, not a real bee's cryptochrome.
keywords:
  - "symmetry-entropy"
  - "orbit-entropy"
  - "projection-entropy"
  - "asymmetry-cost"
  - "von-neumann-entropy"
  - "twirl"
